---
// <BcnFootprintMap> — an entity's footprint on a map: points, filled areas, and
// lines, as an inset card that expands to a modal or as a full-width interactive map.
//
// Renamed from BcnComponentMap and generalized on 2026-08-17, when the decomposition
// review found it had become a strict superset of BcnProjectMap without absorbing it.
// It now serves all three surfaces — the project dashboard's boundary + alignment, the
// component index's per-component footprints, and one component's work areas — so the
// name no longer says "component". BcnProjectMap is deleted; what it had that this
// lacked (a LineString layer, legend keys shaped per geometry kind, and a slot for
// "Upload boundary") is folded in as `lines`, `MapLegendRow.shape`, and the
// `modal-actions` slot.
//
// WHAT THE GEOMETRY IS, per caller, because none of it is a surveyed boundary yet:
//   · project    — a centreline through the conveyance corridor buffered ~2.4 km each
//     side, derived from the 231 real DCP geotech coordinates. Stands in for the
//     boundary a project will UPLOAD once the spatial-data epic lands.
//   · component  — the hull of the component's work areas. A Component has NO geometry
//     column at all, and BCN-1584 (which adds one) has zero commits. Work areas are
//     the only real geometry a component owns, already returned by the work-areas
//     endpoint and discarded by every current surface.
//   · work areas — the points themselves, which is what BCN-1583 slice 1 proposes.
// Every caller therefore names its own source in the provenance field rather than
// letting the map imply an authority the data does not have.
//
// THREE geometry kinds, drawn in this order: areas (translucent, so overlap is
// legible), then lines (dashed by default — a derived centreline is not a survey),
// then points on top. The design call was explicit that overlapping components are
// fine and read the way species habitat layers do.
//
// TWO variants:
//   · variant="inset" — a right-rail card (project dashboard, component dashboard):
//     a small non-interactive picture with an expand action that opens the real map
//     in an esa-dialog.
//   · variant="full"  — the components index: the interactive map at full width, no
//     dialog, no heading (the PAGE owns the heading at that size; `title` still
//     names the map for assistive tech).
//
// MULTI-INSTANCE CONTRACT — the thing BcnProjectMap got wrong. That component
// hardcodes every DOM id (`bcn-map-inset`, `bcn-map-dialog`, `bcn-map-full`,
// `bcn-map-expand`, `bcn-map-data`), so a second instance on one page silently
// steals the first one's map. Here every id is namespaced by the REQUIRED
// `idPrefix`, and — because an Astro `<script>` is hoisted and bundled ONCE per
// page rather than re-run per instance — no prop is visible to the controller as
// a closure. Props are threaded through the DOM instead: `data-*` on the root
// plus a sibling `<script type="application/json" data-bcn-fmap-data={idPrefix}>`
// payload (the idiom BcnProjectTimeline and BcnProjectMap already use). The
// module walks every `[data-bcn-fmap]` and builds an independent map per root.
//
// Three Leaflet gotchas — the first two recorded in the project-map handoff,
// the third found rendering this component on the components index:
//   1. `setView()` must be called BEFORE any layer is added, otherwise Leaflet
//      throws on the first tile; `fitBounds()` then takes over.
//   2. the modal's map is created LAZILY on first open (a map built in a
//      display:none dialog measures 0×0 and renders as a grey box) and
//      `invalidateSize()` runs on every REopen.
//   3. the FULL variant has the same problem without a dialog to hang lazy
//      creation off: built inside a hidden tab/view panel it measures 0×0, so
//      fitBounds resolves against nothing and the map opens zoomed to the middle
//      of the ocean. It therefore watches its own box (ResizeObserver) and
//      re-measures + re-fits the first time it has real size, so a caller never
//      has to remember to poke it on reveal.
//
// Basemap is grayscale on purpose — house rule: containers stay neutral, color
// lives in the data. The only color on this surface is the markers.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: no esa-* map lego exists — `ls
// node_modules/@esa/ecology/src/components/` has nothing map/geo/spatial, and
// the hub's /components esa-map entry is a documentation page with no source
// behind it. Everything AROUND the map is a lego and is used as one: the card
// shell IS esa-card, the expand affordance IS esa-icon-button, the modal IS
// esa-dialog. Checked Beacon prod — its map is an Angular/Leaflet page, not a
// reusable ui-* control. Sibling BcnProjectMap can't be reused (singleton ids,
// boundary/alignment GeoJSON only, "component markers were cut"), and
// BcnObservationMap is severity-pin-shaped with no card/dialog/legend chrome —
// this is the reusable home for a component footprint. The CSS below is the map
// container's own geometry plus the legend key, which no lego models.
import EsaCard from '@esa/ecology/esa-card.astro';
import EsaIconButton from '@esa/ecology/esa-button.astro';
import '../../styles/beacon-map.css';

export interface MapPoint {
  id: string;
  lat: number;
  lon: number;
  /** WorkArea.Status (or any status vocabulary) — mapped to a token below. */
  status?: string;
  /** Tooltip text on the interactive map. Falls back to the id. */
  label?: string;
  /** Explicit override. A TOKEN REFERENCE (`var(--color-background-utility-success)`), never a hex —
   *  the controller resolves var() to a literal because Leaflet paths can't take one. */
  markColor?: string;
}

export interface MapArea {
  id: string;
  /** Closed ring of [lat, lon] pairs. */
  ring: [number, number][];
  /** Tooltip text. Falls back to the id. */
  label?: string;
  /** A TOKEN REFERENCE (`var(--bcn-status-in-progress)`), never a hex. */
  color?: string;
}

export interface MapLine {
  id: string;
  /** Open path of [lat, lon] pairs — a corridor centreline, an alignment, a reach. */
  path: [number, number][];
  label?: string;
  /** A TOKEN REFERENCE, never a hex. */
  color?: string;
  /** Dashed by default: a derived or planned line should not read as a surveyed one. */
  solid?: boolean;
}

/**
 * A legend row. `shape` matters because the three geometry kinds do not read as the
 * same swatch — a dot for a point, a bordered block for a filled area, a dashed rule
 * for a line. BcnProjectMap drew its two keys by hand for exactly this reason; making
 * shape a prop is what let that component be absorbed rather than kept.
 */
export interface MapLegendRow {
  label: string;
  color: string;
  shape?: 'dot' | 'area' | 'line';
}

interface Props {
  /** Points to plot. For the detail page, one component's work areas. */
  points?: MapPoint[];
  /** Filled rings drawn under the points. For the index, one footprint per component. */
  areas?: MapArea[];
  /** Paths drawn over the areas. For the project, the tunnel alignment. */
  lines?: MapLine[];
  /** 'inset' = small non-interactive card that expands to a modal; 'full' = large interactive map. */
  variant?: 'inset' | 'full';
  title?: string;
  /** Namespaces every DOM id so two instances can coexist. REQUIRED — no singletons. */
  idPrefix: string;
  /** Rendered as a field on the card, never as a caption. e.g. 'Work area locations (35)'. */
  sourceLabel?: string;
  /** The provenance field's LABEL — 'Geometry source' here, 'Boundary source' for a project. */
  sourceName?: string;
  /** Optional legend rows — color is a TOKEN reference. */
  legend?: MapLegendRow[];
}

const {
  points = [],
  areas = [],
  lines = [],
  variant = 'inset',
  title = 'Component footprint',
  idPrefix,
  sourceLabel,
  sourceName = 'Geometry source',
  legend = [],
} = Astro.props;

// Status → SEMANTIC token. Keyed lowercase so 'In progress' / 'in progress' /
// 'IN PROGRESS' all land. Zero literals: every value is a token reference, and
// the --bcn-status-* layer already re-points to the status-color standard.
const STATUS_COLOR: Record<string, string> = {
  cleared: 'var(--color-background-utility-success)',
  complete: 'var(--bcn-status-completed)',
  completed: 'var(--bcn-status-completed)',
  scheduled: 'var(--color-background-utility-info)',
  active: 'var(--color-background-utility-info)',
  'in progress': 'var(--bcn-status-in-progress)',
  'not started': 'var(--bcn-status-not-started)',
  'on hold': 'var(--bcn-status-not-started)',
  overdue: 'var(--bcn-status-overdue)',
};
const FALLBACK_COLOR = 'var(--color-content-default-tertiary)';

const payload = {
  points: points.map((p) => ({
    id: p.id,
    lat: p.lat,
    lon: p.lon,
    label: p.label ?? p.id,
    color: p.markColor ?? STATUS_COLOR[(p.status ?? '').trim().toLowerCase()] ?? FALLBACK_COLOR,
  })),
  areas: areas.map((a) => ({
    id: a.id,
    ring: a.ring,
    label: a.label ?? a.id,
    color: a.color ?? FALLBACK_COLOR,
  })),
  lines: lines.map((l) => ({
    id: l.id,
    path: l.path,
    label: l.label ?? l.id,
    color: l.color ?? FALLBACK_COLOR,
    solid: l.solid === true,
  })),
};

const count = points.length + areas.length;
const noun = areas.length > 0 && points.length === 0 ? 'footprint' : 'location';
const mapLabel =
  count === 0 ? `${title} — nothing to show` : `${title} — ${count} ${noun}${count === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;

const insetId = `${idPrefix}-inset`;
const fullId = `${idPrefix}-full`;
const dialogId = `${idPrefix}-dialog`;
const expandId = `${idPrefix}-expand`;
---

<div
  class="bcn-fmap"
  id={`${idPrefix}-root`}
  data-bcn-fmap
  data-prefix={idPrefix}
  data-variant={variant}
>
  {
    variant === 'inset' ? (
      <EsaCard title={title}>
        {/* esa-icon-button doesn't forward `id`, so the host span carries it — repo idiom. */}
        <span slot="actions" id={expandId}>
          <EsaIconButton variant="chrome" iconOnly icon="expand" label={`Expand ${title.toLowerCase()} map`} size="sm" />
        </span>

        <div class="stack" data-gap="sm">
          <div class="bcn-fmap__surface bcn-fmap__surface--inset" id={insetId} role="img" aria-label={mapLabel}></div>
          {sourceLabel && (
            <p class="bcn-fmap__source">
              <span class="bcn-fmap__source-label">{sourceName}</span>
              <span class="bcn-fmap__source-value">{sourceLabel}</span>
            </p>
          )}
        </div>
      </EsaCard>
    ) : (
      <div class="stack" data-gap="sm">
        <div
          class="bcn-fmap__surface bcn-fmap__surface--full"
          id={fullId}
          role="region"
          aria-label={mapLabel}
        ></div>
        {(legend.length > 0 || sourceLabel) && (
          <div class="bcn-fmap__foot">
            {legend.length > 0 && (
              <ul class="cluster bcn-fmap__legend" data-gap="md">
                {legend.map((row) => (
                  <li class="bcn-fmap__legend-row">
                    <span
                      class="bcn-fmap__key"
                      data-shape={row.shape ?? 'dot'}
                      style={`--_cmap-key: ${row.color};`}
                      aria-hidden="true"
                    />
                    {row.label}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            )}
            {sourceLabel && (
              <p class="bcn-fmap__source">
                <span class="bcn-fmap__source-label">{sourceName}</span>
                <span class="bcn-fmap__source-value">{sourceLabel}</span>
              </p>
            )}
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    )
  }

  {
    variant === 'inset' && (
      <esa-dialog id={dialogId} heading={title} size="lg" style="--z-modal: 1300; --z-modal-backdrop: 1250;">
        <div class="bcn-fmap__surface bcn-fmap__surface--modal" id={fullId}></div>
        <div slot="footer" class="bcn-fmap__modal-foot">
          {legend.length > 0 && (
            <ul class="cluster bcn-fmap__legend" data-gap="md">
              {legend.map((row) => (
                <li class="bcn-fmap__legend-row">
                  <span
                    class="bcn-fmap__key"
                    data-shape={row.shape ?? 'dot'}
                    style={`--_cmap-key: ${row.color};`}
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  {row.label}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          )}
          {/* Where a caller puts an action that belongs to the geometry itself —
              the project map's "Upload boundary" is the case this exists for. */}
          <slot name="modal-actions" />
        </div>
      </esa-dialog>
    )
  }
</div>

<script
  type="application/json"
  data-bcn-fmap-data={idPrefix}
  set:html={JSON.stringify(payload)}
></script>

<script>
  import L from 'leaflet';
  import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-dialog';

  interface MapPoint {
    id: string;
    lat: number;
    lon: number;
    label: string;
    /** Token reference (`var(--color-background-utility-success)`) or a literal. */
    color: string;
  }

  interface MapArea {
    id: string;
    ring: [number, number][];
    label: string;
    color: string;
  }

  interface MapLine {
    id: string;
    path: [number, number][];
    label: string;
    color: string;
    solid: boolean;
  }

  interface MapData {
    points: MapPoint[];
    areas: MapArea[];
    lines: MapLine[];
  }

  type CmapRoot = HTMLElement & { _bcnCmapReady?: boolean };
  type CmapDialog = HTMLElement & { open: boolean; show?: () => void };

  /** Statewide California — the neutral view when there is nothing to fit. */
  const EMPTY_VIEW: [number, number] = [37.6, -120.4];
  const EMPTY_ZOOM = 5;
  const MARK_FALLBACK = '#8a9099';

  const rootStyle = () => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);

  /**
   * Leaflet paths take LITERAL colors, so a `var(--color-background-utility-success)` prop has to be
   * resolved first. Recurses because a semantic token may alias another var(),
   * and honors an inline var() fallback.
   */
  function resolveColor(value: string, depth = 0): string {
    const raw = (value || '').trim();
    if (!raw || depth > 4) return MARK_FALLBACK;
    const m = raw.match(/^var\(\s*(--[\w-]+)\s*(?:,\s*([\s\S]+))?\)$/);
    if (!m) return raw;
    const resolved = rootStyle().getPropertyValue(m[1]).trim();
    if (resolved) return resolveColor(resolved, depth + 1);
    return m[2] ? resolveColor(m[2], depth + 1) : MARK_FALLBACK;
  }

  /** Grayscale basemap — the container stays neutral so the markers carry the color. */
  const basemap = () =>
    L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/light_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', {
      attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO',
      subdomains: 'abcd',
      maxZoom: 19,
    });

  const INSET_OPTIONS: L.MapOptions = {
    zoomControl: false,
    attributionControl: false,
    dragging: false,
    scrollWheelZoom: false,
    doubleClickZoom: false,
    boxZoom: false,
    keyboard: false,
    touchZoom: false,
  };

  const LIVE_OPTIONS: L.MapOptions = { zoomControl: true, attributionControl: true };

  const EMPTY: MapData = { points: [], areas: [], lines: [] };

  function readData(prefix: string): MapData {
    const el = document.querySelector(`[data-bcn-fmap-data="${prefix}"]`);
    if (!el) return EMPTY;
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(el.textContent || 'null');
      if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== 'object') return EMPTY;
      return {
        points: Array.isArray(parsed.points) ? parsed.points : [],
        areas: Array.isArray(parsed.areas) ? parsed.areas : [],
        lines: Array.isArray(parsed.lines) ? parsed.lines : [],
      };
    } catch {
      return EMPTY;
    }
  }

  /** Every coordinate on the map — what the view has to contain. */
  const extentOf = (d: MapData): L.LatLngTuple[] => [
    ...d.points.map((p) => [p.lat, p.lon] as L.LatLngTuple),
    ...d.areas.flatMap((a) => a.ring.map((r) => [r[0], r[1]] as L.LatLngTuple)),
    ...d.lines.flatMap((l) => l.path.map((r) => [r[0], r[1]] as L.LatLngTuple)),
  ];

  /** Draw the geometry into `map` and fit the view to it. */
  function plot(map: L.Map, data: MapData, interactive: boolean, pad: number) {
    const stroke = rootStyle().getPropertyValue('--color-background-elevation-raised').trim() || '#ffffff';
    const group = L.layerGroup().addTo(map);

    // Areas first, so points sit ON them. Translucent fill with a solid edge:
    // sixteen overlapping footprints have to stay legible where they stack, and
    // the outline is what keeps each one's shape readable through the pile.
    for (const a of data.areas) {
      const color = resolveColor(a.color);
      const shape = L.polygon(a.ring as L.LatLngExpression[], {
        color,
        weight: interactive ? 2 : 1,
        fillColor: color,
        fillOpacity: 0.18,
        opacity: 0.85,
        interactive,
      });
      if (interactive) {
        shape.bindTooltip(a.label, { sticky: true, direction: 'top' });
        // Bring the hovered footprint forward and firm up its fill — the only way
        // to isolate one shape out of an overlapping stack without a legend click.
        shape.on('mouseover', () => {
          shape.bringToFront();
          shape.setStyle({ fillOpacity: 0.36, weight: 3 });
        });
        shape.on('mouseout', () => shape.setStyle({ fillOpacity: 0.18, weight: 2 }));
      }
      shape.addTo(group);
    }

    // Lines over areas, under points: an alignment should read as crossing its
    // footprints, and dashed by default because a derived centreline is not a survey.
    for (const l of data.lines) {
      const color = resolveColor(l.color);
      const line = L.polyline(l.path as L.LatLngExpression[], {
        color,
        weight: interactive ? 3 : 2,
        opacity: 0.9,
        dashArray: l.solid ? undefined : '5 5',
        interactive,
      });
      if (interactive) line.bindTooltip(l.label, { sticky: true, direction: 'top' });
      line.addTo(group);
    }

    for (const p of data.points) {
      const marker = L.circleMarker([p.lat, p.lon], {
        // Modest: a footprint reads as a scatter of sites, not a pin cushion.
        radius: interactive ? 6 : 4,
        color: stroke,
        weight: interactive ? 2 : 1,
        fillColor: resolveColor(p.color),
        fillOpacity: 0.9,
        interactive,
      });
      if (interactive) marker.bindTooltip(p.label, { sticky: true, direction: 'top' });
      marker.addTo(group);
    }

    const extent = extentOf(data);
    if (extent.length > 0) {
      map.fitBounds(L.latLngBounds(extent), { padding: [pad, pad], maxZoom: 14 });
    }
  }

  /**
   * Gotcha 3 — a map built inside a HIDDEN container measures 0x0, so its
   * fitBounds resolves against nothing and it comes back as a grey square zoomed
   * to the middle of the ocean. The components index builds this map inside a
   * hidden view panel, and the same is true of any tab or accordion host.
   *
   * Rather than making every caller remember to poke the map on reveal, the map
   * watches its OWN box: the first time it has real size, it re-measures and
   * re-fits. Cheap, self-contained, and correct for hosts that have not been
   * written yet.
   */
  function refitWhenSized(map: L.Map, el: HTMLElement, data: MapData, pad: number) {
    if (typeof ResizeObserver === 'undefined') return;
    let settled = el.clientWidth > 0 && el.clientHeight > 0;
    const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
      const sized = el.clientWidth > 0 && el.clientHeight > 0;
      if (!sized || settled) return;
      settled = true;
      map.invalidateSize();
      const extent = extentOf(data);
      if (extent.length > 0) {
        map.fitBounds(L.latLngBounds(extent), { padding: [pad, pad], maxZoom: 14 });
      }
      ro.disconnect();
    });
    ro.observe(el);
  }

  function build(root: CmapRoot) {
    if (root._bcnCmapReady) return;
    root._bcnCmapReady = true;

    const prefix = root.dataset.prefix || '';
    const variant = root.dataset.variant === 'full' ? 'full' : 'inset';
    const data = readData(prefix);

    if (variant === 'full') {
      const el = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-full`);
      if (!el) return;
      // Gotcha 1: a view must exist BEFORE any layer is added.
      const map = L.map(el, LIVE_OPTIONS).setView(EMPTY_VIEW, EMPTY_ZOOM);
      basemap().addTo(map);
      plot(map, data, true, 24);
      requestAnimationFrame(() => map.invalidateSize());
      refitWhenSized(map, el, data, 24);
      return;
    }

    // ── Inset: a picture of the footprint, no interaction ──
    const insetEl = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-inset`);
    if (insetEl) {
      const inset = L.map(insetEl, INSET_OPTIONS).setView(EMPTY_VIEW, EMPTY_ZOOM);
      basemap().addTo(inset);
      plot(inset, data, false, 10);
      requestAnimationFrame(() => inset.invalidateSize());
    }

    // ── Modal: the interactive map, built on FIRST open (gotcha 2) ──
    const dialog = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-dialog`) as CmapDialog | null;
    const expand = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-expand`);
    if (!dialog || !expand) return;

    let full: L.Map | null = null;
    expand.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (dialog.show) dialog.show();
      else dialog.open = true;
      requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        if (!full) {
          const el = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-full`);
          if (!el) return;
          full = L.map(el, LIVE_OPTIONS).setView(EMPTY_VIEW, EMPTY_ZOOM);
          basemap().addTo(full);
          plot(full, data, true, 24);
        } else {
          // A map hidden since last close remembers a stale size — re-measure.
          full.invalidateSize();
        }
      });
    });
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<CmapRoot>('[data-bcn-fmap]').forEach(build);
</script>

<style>
  /* Map-container geometry only — rounded, clipped, sunken while tiles load;
     the same treatment BcnProjectMap and BcnObservationMap give their surfaces. */
  .bcn-fmap__surface {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius-200);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken);
  }

  /* Rail inset — a fixed band that reads as a picture. */
  .bcn-fmap__surface--inset {
    height: 180px;
  }

  /* Full page view and the modal both hold a generous FIXED frame that never
     resizes on interaction (design-principles: stabilize the frame). */
  .bcn-fmap__surface--full {
    height: min(64vh, 560px);
  }
  .bcn-fmap__surface--modal {
    height: min(70vh, 620px);
  }

  /* Leaflet injects .leaflet-container itself, so it is outside Astro's scope. */
  .bcn-fmap__surface :global(.leaflet-container) {
    font-family: var(--typography-font-family-sans, inherit);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken);
  }
  /* A picture must not offer a grab cursor it won't honor. */
  .bcn-fmap__surface--inset :global(.leaflet-container) {
    cursor: default;
  }
  .bcn-fmap__surface :global(.leaflet-interactive) {
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Provenance is a FIELD (label + value), never a caption under the map — once
     the boundary epic lands this same slot names the uploaded geometry. */
  .bcn-fmap__source {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem; /* 13px — the meta floor */
  }
  .bcn-fmap__source-label {
    color: var(--color-content-default-tertiary);
  }
  .bcn-fmap__source-value {
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-medium);
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
  }

  .bcn-fmap__foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--spacing-400);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* The modal footer: legend left, any geometry action (e.g. "Upload boundary")
     right — the Windows order this house follows puts the action group last. */
  .bcn-fmap__modal-foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--spacing-400);
    width: 100%;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .bcn-fmap__legend {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: var(--font-size-150);
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
  }
  /* In BOTH footers the legend sits beside something else, so it must not claim the
     full width — otherwise it pushes the sibling action onto its own row. */
  .bcn-fmap__foot .bcn-fmap__legend,
  .bcn-fmap__modal-foot .bcn-fmap__legend {
    width: auto;
  }
